an overworked pig, a soulful gorilla, a punk-rock

00:00:06.141 --> 00:00:09.920
porcupine, and an egotistical mouse are just
some of the characters you'll meet in the

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.910
animated musical movie, Sing.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.020
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here!

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.660
And in this video, I'm going to be revealing
behind-the-scenes secrets and facts about

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.370
the movie Sing including some cool easter
eggs.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.580
Just before I start, I've got a giveaway for
some awesome Sing merchandise.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.740
All you need to do for a chance to win is
subscribe and leave a comment on this video

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.251
about your favourite song, character or easter
egg from the movie.

00:00:31.251 --> 00:00:34.660
For details about the prizes and bonus ways
to enter the giveaway, check out the Gleam

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.930
link in the video description below.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:40.510
And if you've not seen the movie, just to
let you know there are spoilers ahead.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:45.110
Ok, now, let's take a look at 17 fun facts
and easter eggs in the movie Sing.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.940
For the soulful-singing gorilla Johnny, the
filmmakers channelled Michael J Fox's Marty

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.350
McFly from Back to the Future.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:55.890
But that's just the start of Sing's hat-tips
to the iconic mid-80s movie.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.600
Remember when the theatre's electricity suddenly
shuts down?

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.550
Well, Buster tries to get the power back on
by climbing out onto the theatre's façade

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:06.889
while pulling an electric cable from his building
and trying to connect it to a cable from the

00:01:06.889 --> 00:01:08.030
building next door.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:12.430
But like Doc, at the end of Back to the Future,
Buster's cable doesn't quite reach, and needs

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:13.430
an extra tug.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:18.579
Oh, and did you notice the hands of the clock
outside Buster's theatre are on 10 and 12,

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:21.610
a shout-out to the scene in Back to the Future?

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:26.070
And in Sing's finale, when the punk-rocking
porcupine Ash performs 'Set It All Free',

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:30.530
she finishes with a final flourish on her
guitar as she knee-slides across the stage,

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:35.259
then she opens her eyes to find the audience
in stunned silence, which is a nod to Marty

00:01:35.259 --> 00:01:39.649
McFly's guitar-heavy, knee-sliding performance
of Johnny B Good in Back to the Future.

00:01:39.649 --> 00:01:44.139
The inspiration behind Sing and its characters
comes from a variety of places, including

00:01:44.139 --> 00:01:47.109
Alan Parker's 1991 hit musical The Commitments.

00:01:47.109 --> 00:01:52.759
And for the character of Gunter, a sparkly-spandex-wearing
pig whose dance performances are super-high

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:57.289
on energy, the filmmakers took cues from Brad
Pitt's personal trainer character in the Coen

00:01:57.289 --> 00:01:59.009
Brother's comedy Burn After Reading.

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:04.619
As for Rosita, an overburdened mother to 25
piglets, Sing's writer-director Garth Jennings

00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:08.649
based her on his own wife, who left her job
as a fashion designer to raise their four

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:14.150
children and, like Rosita, faced self-doubt
when she decided to return to her former profession.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:19.110
Sing also includes a couple of easter eggs
to another of Illumination's animated movies,

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:23.270
The Secret Life of Pets, which is especially
nice because, if you remember, a poster for

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.630
Sing appeared on the back of the bus in that
movie!

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:30.490
Ok, first up, when Sing's bank-robbing gorilla
gang turns up, they're wearing masks that

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:34.780
look just like the crazy bunny Snowball, who's
the leader of The Flushed Pets gang in The

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.650
Secret Life of Pets.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:40.780
And in another hat-tip to that movie, there's
a crocodile called Derek in both films!

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:46.130
In Sing, Derek works at the casino frequented
by Mike, the tiny mouse with an enormous ego.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:50.260
And in The Secret Life of Pets, Derick is
a member of the Flushed Pets gang.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.970
During the five years it took to bring the
final film to life, Sing went through various

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.670
changes and there were a number of rejected
concepts.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:01.040
For example, when the filmmakers first came
up with the idea of the theatre-owning koala

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:05.610
Buster Moon, he was much more of a full-on
con artist than he is in the final movie.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:10.260
However, as they developed the movie, they
realised that over-emphasising Buster's swindling

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.400
ways and bad manners was making him way too
unlikable.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.740
So, they dialled down that aspect of his character.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:20.390
Another character who went through a big change
during the making of the movie was a bullish

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:25.030
business mogul who, up until late in the film's
development, was going to be a big part of

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.030
the story.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:30.220
But in the end, the filmmakers decided he
wasn't necessary to the plot, so his character

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:34.600
had a major downgrade and now you can only
see him in one scene, which is at the bank

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:39.490
where he gives a credit card to the Sinatra-singing
mouse Mike, who's voiced by Seth Macfarlane.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:45.220
As well as directing Sing, Garth Jennings
also provides the voice of Buster's assistant,

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.550
the elderly lizard, Miss Crawly!

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:52.319
And keeping it in the family, Jenning's four
sons, Oscar, Leo, Caspar, and Asa all pop

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:54.620
up in the film, voicing piglets!

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:58.910
As does Asher Blinkoff, whose voice you'll
know best as Dracula's grandson Dennis in

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:01.340
the animated movie Hotel Transylvania 2.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:05.880
By the way, did you spot that the speaking
voice of theatrical diva Nana Noodleman is

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:11.040
provided by Absolutely Fabulous star Jennifer
Saunders, who also voiced the Queen of England

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.980
in Illumination's Minions movie?

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:17.849
But when she's singing, Nana owes her voice
to Dreamgirls star Jennifer Hudson!

00:04:17.849 --> 00:04:23.259
The Grand Budapest Hotel director Wes Anderson
also cameos as a giraffe called Daniel, who

00:04:23.259 --> 00:04:27.259
Buster axes after the auditions because they
can't hear each other due to the difference

00:04:27.259 --> 00:04:28.560
in their heights.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.980
The voices of Despicable Me director Chris
Renaud and Scott Pilgrim vs the World director

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:35.830
Edgar Wright also appear briefly in Sing.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:40.900
Sing is absolutely jam-packed with music,
with over 65 songs, covering everything from

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:44.199
Lady Gaga and John Legend to Frank Sinatra
and The Beatles.

00:04:44.199 --> 00:04:48.539
However, one particular track, Elton John's
I'm Still Standing, proved especially tough

00:04:48.539 --> 00:04:52.819
to get permission to use, taking six months
to get the go-ahead as, at the time, Elton

00:04:52.819 --> 00:04:56.940
John's company Rocket Pictures was thinking
of using it for their own animated movie,

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.990
the Gnomeo &amp; Juliet sequel, Sherlock Gnomes.

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:04.009
The final thing that sealed the deal in Sing's
favour was director Garth Jennings meeting

00:05:04.009 --> 00:05:08.569
David Furnish, Elton John's husband and co-chief
at Rocket Pictures, and showing him the scene

00:05:08.569 --> 00:05:12.800
where Taron Egerton's character Johnny belts
out the song in the movie.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:17.879
Speaking of Taron Egerton, although Sing is
his first full-on musical experience on the

00:05:17.879 --> 00:05:21.220
big screen, Egerton grew up singing and touring
in school choirs and, while he was training

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:26.199
at London's prestigious Royal Academy of Dramatic
Art, he won the Stephen Sondheim Society 'Student

00:05:26.199 --> 00:05:30.270
Performer of the Year' award for his rendition
of two musical numbers including 'Giants in

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.669
the Sky' from Sondheim's Into The Woods.

00:05:32.669 --> 00:05:37.440
However, as Sing's director had never heard
Egerton's vocals before, the Kingsman: Secret

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:41.389
Service star auditioned for the part of Johnny
by performing one of his favourite songs,

00:05:41.389 --> 00:05:43.999
Otis Redding's These Arms of Mine.

00:05:43.999 --> 00:05:47.780
By the way, if you were wondering about those
five brightly-dressed red pandas who pop up

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:51.610
singing and dancing several times during the
movie, they're a shout-out to the music of

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:55.219
the Japanese pop and fashion phenomenon that
is Kyary Pamyu Pamyu.

